        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0615" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg519"/>

                <head>No. 308.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 18, 1874</date>.
                        (Received August 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 590.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Moran’s Nos. 478 and
                    498, I have the honor to forward herewith two copies of the report of Commodore
                    Goodenough and Mr. Consul Layard on the offer of the cession of the Fiji Islands
                    to the British Crown,” just presented to both houses of Parliament by command of
                    the Queen, together with a report, taken from the Times of this morning, of the
                    proceedings in the House of Lords last night on the subject of this
                    annexation.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d310-a1.xml" xpointer="d310-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d310-a2.xml" xpointer="d310-a2"/>
